<title>USA: American Precision buys heat transfer unit.</title>
<headline>American Precision buys heat transfer unit.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO, N.Y. 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Precision Industries Inc said on Tuesday that it has signed a letter of intent to buy Schmidt-Bretten GmbH, a heat transfer subsidiary of KHD Humboldt Wedag AG, for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>Schmidt-Bretten makes Plate and Frame Heat Exchangers, which use water to cool processed fluids, for the chemical and food and beverage industries under the SIGMA trademark. It has annual sales of about $28 million and 120 employees, American said.</p>
<p>The transaction should close at the end of this year, American said.</p>
</text>
